\section{Overlap notation}
Let $X$ and $Y$ name two collections. In the same paragraph, $X$ and $Y$ are also used for events, and no universe or probability space is declared.
The worksheet asks for $X\cap Y$ without choosing between set overlap and event conjunction.

\section{Binary calibration}
Let $ybin\in\{0,1\}$ be a binary label, let $pbin\in(0,1)$ be its predicted probability, and define $Jbin$ as binary cross-entropy loss.
\[Jbin=-ybin\log pbin-(1-ybin)\log(1-pbin).\]

