\section{Source}
The template receives $Fgen$, $qgen$, and $Egen$ without semantic declarations.

\newcommand{\forcecell}[3]{#1=#2#3}
\section{Generated supplement}
The macro arguments remain semantically undeclared.
\[\forcecell{Fgen}{qgen}{Egen}\]

\def\opaqueB#1{\csname hiddenB\endcsname{#1}}
The macro body is deliberately opaque to bounded structural expansion.

\[
\opaqueB{\tau_B=\mu_B\dot\gamma_B}
\]

No editable generated child or guessed constitutive meaning is authorized.

\newcommand{\evolveB}[3]{#1_t=#2\nabla^2 #1}
Let $u_B$ be a differentiable temperature field, $t_B$ time, and $k_B$ measured diffusivity.

\[
\evolveB{u_B}{k_B}{t_B}
\]

The old transparent definition omitted an explicit time argument.

\newcommand{\evolveB}[3]{\frac{\partial #1}{\partial #3}=#2\nabla^2 #1}
Let $u_B$ be a differentiable temperature field, $t_B$ time, and $k_B$ measured diffusivity.

\[
\evolveB{u_B}{k_B}{t_B}
\]

The relinked transparent expansion is current, while its generated children remain noneditable.
